# CH19 — The Hand That Wrote the Seal. Whitebone sanctuary: cells opened by consent, SC10.

@scene CH19_ARRIVE once
say narr | Whitebone's snow gate. The redoubt's cells are a sanctuary now - doors propped open, blankets on the bunks. Except three.
say oriel | Oni?
say sable | Here. Don't come in with weapons out. Some of them flinch.
say sable | Three people still wear bindings I wrote. I can't take them off alone. If I get the key wrong, the seal repeats its command. I won't risk that on someone else's body.
say sable | I've already sent my name and testimony to Nacre. Whatever they decide, I'll answer it. But first - these three.
objective oriel | Open the three sealed cells one by one. Ask each person for their own consent key, then use it at their lock.
@end

@scene CH19_KEEPER
say monk | The sanctuary keeps no records of who is 'guilty'. Only who needs a blanket.
@end

@scene CH19_SURVIVOR_GATE
say survivor | You're with him? ...I'll watch. That's all.
@end

@scene CH19_SABLE
if flag:d07p_open1,flag:d07p_open2,flag:d07p_open3 done
say sable | Ask them. Not me. I only know the command I wrote. They know who they are.
end
label done
say sable | That's all three. I - thank you. No. That's not for me to say.
@end

@scene CH19_CELL1
if flag:d07p_key1 given
say survivor | You want my key? It was a number, once. Warrant 4-11.
say survivor | ...My name is Hesk. That's the key. Hesk. Say it right.
set d07p_key1
end
label given
say survivor | Hesk. Go on. The lock's outside.
@end

@scene CH19_CELL2
if flag:d07p_key2 given
say elder | Seventy years I've had this seal. I'm not sure I remember my own name.
say oriel | Then choose one. It doesn't have to be old to be yours.
say elder | ...Wren. Old woman, new name. Wren.
set d07p_key2
end
label given
say elder | Wren. I like how it sounds in someone else's mouth when they ask.
@end

@scene CH19_CELL3
if flag:d07p_key3 given
say patient | I don't want it off yet.
say oriel | Then it stays on until you do.
wait 0.5
say patient | ...That's the first time anyone's said that. All right. Now. Key's 'Tamsin'. Now.
set d07p_key3
end
label given
say patient | Tamsin. Quickly, before I change my mind. Or don't - I'm allowed to change it.
@end

@scene CH19_LOCK1
if flag:d07p_open1 done
if !flag:d07p_key1 nokey
sfx FX024
say narr | The seal hears 'Hesk', spoken the way he asked, and lets go. The cell door swings wide.
set d07p_open1
call CH19_CELLS
end
label nokey
say narr | The lock waits for a key. Only the person inside can give it.
end
label done
say narr | The cell is open.
@end

@scene CH19_LOCK2
if flag:d07p_open2 done
if !flag:d07p_key2 nokey
sfx FX024
say narr | 'Wren.' The seal hesitates, as if surprised to hear a name it has never known, then releases.
set d07p_open2
call CH19_CELLS
end
label nokey
say narr | The lock waits for a key. Only the person inside can give it.
end
label done
say narr | The cell is open.
@end

@scene CH19_LOCK3
if flag:d07p_open3 done
if !flag:d07p_key3 nokey
sfx FX024
say narr | 'Tamsin.' The binding unwinds. The door opens. Tamsin stays inside for a moment, then walks out on her own.
set d07p_open3
call CH19_CELLS
end
label nokey
say narr | The lock waits for a key. Only the person inside can give it.
end
label done
say narr | The cell is open.
@end

@scene CH19_CELLS
if flag:d07p_open1,flag:d07p_open2,flag:d07p_open3 all
end
label all
objective oriel | All three cells are open. Walk Oni out to the sanctuary exit.
@end

@scene CH19_SC10 once
show surv10 19 20 up survivor
say survivor | You wrote my number.
say sable | Yes.
say survivor | You remember it.
say sable | Yes.
say survivor | Do you know my name?
say sable | Not yet.
say survivor | Then start there.
say sable | May I write it down?
wait 0.8
say survivor | ...Ilse. With an s.
say narr | Oni writes it. The survivor watches him do it, and does not say thank you, and walks away.
hide surv10
say sable | Before I go back to Nacre for the hearing - Voss's network. If there's any way to stop it from compelling anyone again, I want to help.
say oriel | The survivors decide that.
say narr | In the sanctuary hall, the survivors talk it over without him. They come back with a single page: a limited agreement. He may help. They keep a copy of his account.
set sable_agreement
if party:C03 correnline
goto correndone
label correnline
say corren | You let someone else hold the lever. Took me years to learn that.
label correndone
if party:C08 pipline
goto pipdone
label pipline
say pip | Blank forms and a proper seal. Welcome to paperwork that doesn't hurt anyone.
label pipdone
join C07
call OV_KITSUNE_BACK
chapter CH19
objective dain | Oni is back, under the survivors' agreement.
call REUNION_CHECK
level_floor 29
@end
